Q: How to identify server IP address in PHP A: <p>If you used some methods to get the PHP Server Public IP Address and you cannot still get the correct Server Public IP Address, you can use file_get_content() function.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php
$FCData = []; $FCData['JSONDataKey'] = 'String';
$Header = (array(&quot;Accept: application/json&quot;, &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot;, &quot;Authorization: MyAuthorizationHeaderKey&quot;));
$Option = array('http' =&gt; array('header' =&gt; $Header, 'method' =&gt; 'POST', 'content' =&gt; json_encode($FCData), 'ignore_errors' =&gt; true ));
$Context = stream_context_create($Option);
$FCResData = file_get_contents('https:/mywebsiteurl.com/dirfolder/GetMyServerIPAddress.php', false, $Context);
?&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>This is for GetMyMyServerIPAddress.php</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php
/** This is GetMyMyServerIPAddress.php */

$RequestHeaders = getallheaders(); $Post = file_get_contents('php://input');
// echo json_encode($RequestHeaders).'&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;'.$Post; exit;
if(isset($RequestHeaders['Authorization']) &amp;&amp; $RequestHeaders['Authorization'] == 'AuthorizationKey' &amp;&amp; isset($RequestHeaders['Content-Type']) &amp;&amp; stristr($RequestHeaders['Content-Type'], 'json')){
   $MyServerIPAddress = GetMyServerIPAddress(); $ServerIPv4Address = ''; $ServerIPv6Address = 'N/A';
   if(mb_strlen($MyServerIPAddress &lt; 15)){
      $ServerIPv4Address = $MyServerIPAddress;
   }
   else{
      $ServerIPv4Address = gethostbyname($_SERVER['HTTP_HOST']); $ServerIPv6Address = $MyServerIPAddress;
   }

   $ResData = []; $ResData['GSHIPA'] = ''; $ResData['ServerIPv4Address'] = $ServerIPv4Address; $ResData['ServerIPv6Address'] = $ServerIPv6Address; echo json_encode($ResData);
}

function GetMyServerIPAddress(){
   if(!empty($_SERVER['HTTP_CLIENT_IP'])){ 
      $IP = $_SERVER['HTTP_CLIENT_IP']; 
   }
   elseif(!empty($_SERVER['HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR'])){ 
      $IP = $_SERVER['HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR']; 
   }
   else{ 
      $IP = $_SERVER['REMOTE_ADDR']; 
   } 

   if( filter_var($IP, FILTER_VALIDATE_IP, FILTER_FLAG_IPV4 | FILTER_FLAG_IPV6 | FILTER_FLAG_NO_PRIV_RANGE | FILTER_FLAG_NO_RES_RANGE) === false ){
      return 'n/a';
   }
   else{
      return $IP;
   }
} // End of function GetMyServerIPAddress()
?&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: I need an example of a chart.js that resizes correctly in a Bootstrap grid layout A: <p>The chart can only resize if its parent container provides enough height <em>and</em> width; and at the same time the container (in this case the height of the grid row) shrinks to fit the size of the chart. This is fine while the size is decreasing... but when the window expands there's a problem. The chart can't resize because the container is too small, and the container won't grow because the content hasn't resized. Deadlock.</p>
<p>Most published solutions seem to rely on setting a fixed height for the grid row, but this doesn't really work if you want to maintain the aspect ratio of chart <em>and</em> avoid a gap above or below the chart.</p>
<p>The solution I've currently arrived at, as shown in the snippet, is to listen for the <code>window.resize</code> and then set the correct height for the parent container in relation to its new width. This breaks the deadlock and allows the chart to expand.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const myCanvas = document.getElementById('canvas-id');
const chartRow = document.getElementById('chart-row-id');
const chartCol = document.getElementById('chart-col-id');

// create the chart as normal
const myChart = new Chart(myCanvas, {
  type: 'bar',
  data: {
    labels: ['a', 'b', 'c'],
    datasets: [{
      label: 'Sample data',
      data: [3, 4, 2]
    }]
  },
  options: {
    maintainAspectRatio: true,
    aspectRatio: 3.5, // (optional, if desired)
    responsive: true,
    plugins: {
      legend: {
        display: false
      }
    }
  }
});

// THIS IS THE IMPORTANT BIT
// --------------------------------------------
// The chart will only resize if its parent row
// provides enough vertical space. So here we 
// react to the Window resize event and set the
// row to the correct height for the chart.
// --------------------------------------------
addEventListener('resize', e =&gt; {
  // calculate chart column content width
  const style = getComputedStyle(chartCol);
  const contentWidth = chartCol.clientWidth
    - parseFloat(style.paddingLeft) - parseFloat(style.paddingRight);
  // calculate correct row height for chart
  const rowHeight = Math.floor(contentWidth / myChart.aspectRatio);
  // set row height using an inline style
  chartRow.style = `height: ${rowHeight}px;`;
});</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/Chart.js/4.5.0/chart.umd.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.8/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet" /&gt;

&lt;!-- create the bootstrap grid layout as normal --&gt;
&lt;div class='container-fluid'&gt;
  &lt;h3&gt;Resizable chart example&lt;/h3&gt;

  &lt;div id='chart-row-id' class='row'&gt;
    &lt;div id='chart-col-id' class='col-9'&gt;
      &lt;canvas id='canvas-id'&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class='col-3 bg-warning'&gt;
      next column
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;div class='row'&gt;
    &lt;div class='col-12 bg-info'&gt;
      next row
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
